.TH "GIT-WORK" "1" "Apr 2019" "Generated from git-work's source code" ""

.SH NAME
git-work-flow - List the flows, one line each


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit-work flow [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the flows, one line per flow: the name and the first line
of its description.

.PP
This is the human form of \fBgit work flow list\fR, which prints the same flows
as JSON, their arguments included, and is the form to script against;
--format json prints that here too.

.PP
A flow is one Starlark function stored in refs/work-flows. Its name is the
flow's name, its docstring the description and its parameters the arguments
\fBgit work flow run\fR takes.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-f\fP, \fB--format\fP="text"
	Select the output formatting style. Valid values are [text,json]

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for flow


